{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_124","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nEight blockers remain: five high, three medium. Findings below are based on source inspection; the focused policy tests passed.\n\nExecuted checks:\n\n- Focused policy tests, CLI publication race test, and `go vet`: passed.\n- Artifact-check and surface-check: failed on undeclared `spec.go`.\n- Component validation: 208 passed, one failed, one timed out.\n- Repository validation: 212 passed, one failed.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, and delivery-evidence rules. The worktree remains clean; no attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N9\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 309,\n      \"summary\": \"Removing the current scope-kind profile bypasses protected mandatory-human overlays. Consider an adopted baseline with never, an ordinary base profile, and a selected mandatory-human overlay. A contract-changing scope removes profiles.milestone. protectCloseoutDecision checks baseline policy independence and its base profile, but not baseline overlays; evaluateCloseoutReview(base) returns exempt. mandatoryHumanReview then returns false here without constructing the protected effective plan. ReviewCheck grants the exemption before its missing-profile check. Resolve protected effective independence even when the current profile mapping is absent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N10\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go\",\n      \"line\": 373,\n      \"summary\": \"An exempt multi-member milestone can close without evidence for its exit gate. roadmapGate evaluates cut criteria only for a roadmap and never reads Milestone.ExitGate. The milestone close branch calls this gate and publishes a receipt. The exit-gate judgment otherwise belongs to the skipped aggregate review; addMilestoneGateCriterion carries it into a member review only for a singleton (review_plan.go:1111). Thus a two-member milestone under when-justified, or a multi-member milestone under never, can close with an unsatisfied exit gate. Preserve independent gate verification when aggregate review is exempt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N11\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\",\n      \"line\": 2819,\n      \"summary\": \"Exemption can erase a child-scope blocker based on the child's name. removeReviewOnlyBlockers removes every message containing review, criterion, or finding (line 2983), including 'child spec:review-client is not closed'. After a valid exempt close, a later authentic rejection of that child leaves its status done and the aggregate receipt unchanged. The child becomes nonterminal, but its blocker is removed and the aggregate can still report Terminal=true. MCP and federatedSourceProof consume that false terminal state. Filter typed aggregate-review diagnostics instead of arbitrary message substrings, and retain every child blocker.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N12\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 183,\n      \"summary\": \"Backward Markdown associations still do not resolve their targets. An inventoried ADR containing [program](../roadmaps/missing.md) is silently ignored because its normalized path is not exactly the current roadmapPath. Unlike roadmaps: declarations, missing, ambiguous, or unreadable local Markdown roadmap targets produce no diagnostic. A multi-member roadmap can consequently receive a known when-justified exemption from an incomplete association inventory. Resolve local Markdown association targets before proving absence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N13\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 535,\n      \"summary\": \"closedByReceipt verifies only the aggregate's review, not its terminal closeout. For an exempt receipt without an aggregate review record, reviewCheck returns immediately as not-required without checking children or dependency acceptance. If a member later receives a negative or incomplete review while remaining done, GetCloseoutState reports the child open, but closedByReceipt still returns true. ReachedMilestones, milestoneReachedObligations, and roadmapReachedApartFrom therefore suppress or count a nonterminal scope as closed. Project the applicable terminal verifier rather than only its review half.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N14\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 383,\n      \"summary\": \"Receipt-backed domain terminal verification checks gate text but not whether its evidence still holds. Close an exempt roadmap with C1: manual-review:docs/review.md, then remove that report while retaining the criterion and members. closeoutReceiptStands still succeeds because their digests are unchanged; GetCloseoutState never evaluates cut criteria and can remain terminal, allowing federatedSourceProof to accept the receipt. Repeating CLI close now correctly fails through closeGateBlocker, so the surfaces disagree. Move applicable gate verification into the shared terminal path and preserve historical policy independence separately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N15\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-11-pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit.md\",\n      \"line\": 108,\n      \"summary\": \"The artifact declaration omits modified pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go. The supplied range changes Store by adding planWithoutCloseoutGate, but the Artifacts section does not claim that path. Both required gates exit 1: surface-check reports 'error undeclared pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go'; artifact-check JSON confirms the same undeclared path as its sole error. Declare the exact modification and rerun both strict gates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N16\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 489,\n      \"summary\": \"Previously terminal milestones with their own sealed approval are still reopened when their parent roadmap remains active. closeoutScopeHistorical requires the parent roadmap to be done and never checks the milestone's own positive historical terminal evidence. Adoption therefore sets CloseRequired=true and Terminal=false for a milestone that the prior verifier considered terminal, even when its review and members remain valid. R7 and the technical plan preserve prior terminal history, not only milestones under done roadmaps. Distinguish a historically approved terminal milestone from a merely reached milestone.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F1\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:313 now builds the effective plan, whose overlay selection is composed in review_plan.go:316-350. The missing-current-profile return at closeout_review_policy.go:309 still bypasses protected overlay independence; see N9.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F2\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:370-386 compares canonical members and exit-gate digests without reevaluating current policy; roadmap cut syntax is now bound at line 469. Semantic gate evidence is still not verified by domain terminal readers; see N14.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F3\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:489-514 adds intent checks and positive legacy roadmap evidence. It still requires the parent roadmap to be done, leaving independently approved historical milestones under active roadmaps reopened; see N16. The preservation requirement remains explicit in the spec at line 99.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F5\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:141-158 reads every Markdown candidate, including README.md, and diagnoses regular-file, size, and read failures. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTwo and RoundThree passed in the executed focused suite. N12 concerns a separate unresolved Markdown-target path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F6\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:535 now invokes reviewCheck, and CloseoutReviewsOwed no longer skips every done roadmap. This fixes the recorded-own-review cases, but the helper still omits child and dependency terminal verification; see N13.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:411-431 retains adopted baseline always with enabled=false and loads baseline policy/base-profile human requirements at the baseline revision. Protected overlay independence remains bypassable when the current profile mapping is removed; see N9.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:535-539 verifies the aggregate's applicable review instead of merely checking for a negative verdict. The executed focused suite passed closeout_review_policy_test.go:761, covering a sealed but unattested aggregate review after the receipt. N13 covers the remaining child-terminal projection gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"schemas/v1/closeout-receipt.schema.json:17 declares exit_gate_digest. The executed focused suite passed closeout_review_policy_test.go:793, checking emitted fields against the published schema.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"cli/review_closeout.go:2470-2483 returns read-only verification for an already-terminal historical roadmap and does not construct a recovery receipt. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyHistoricalRoadmapCloseIsReadOnly at cli/closeout_review_policy_test.go:319 passed in the focused suite.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N5\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:173 resolves local roadmaps: targets through GetRoadmap and diagnoses failures. The focused suite passed closeout_review_policy_test.go:747 for a missing backward-declared roadmap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N6\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:141 no longer excludes README.md. The focused suite passed closeout_review_policy_test.go:754, proving that a README backlink contributes an association.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N7\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:313 delegates current overlay applicability to ReviewPlan, including its selectors and adoption cutoff at review_plan.go:316-350. The focused suite passed closeout_review_policy_test.go:662, including the nonselected-overlay case.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N8\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_review_policy.go:469 hashes parsed roadmap cut criteria, and cli/review_closeout.go:2462 reruns the applicable CLI gate on repeated close. The focused suite passed the changed-cut-criteria regression at closeout_review_policy_test.go:776. N14 identifies the separate case of unchanged criteria whose evidence disappears.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the supplied range and spec/ADR, all supplied prior findings, policy schema validation, canonical membership and transfer handling, ADR inventory and both association directions, baseline and effective human independence, voluntary-review vetoes, receipt parsing/publication/history, CLI close and recovery, review-check, review verification, review-plan, closeout state/check, reached/nextCloses, attention/obligations, roadmap-check, MCP projection, federated source acceptance, doctor, adoption/setup/update compatibility, schemas, English/pt-BR docs and scaffold parity. Examined the adversarial corpus: the exempt exit-gate and child-name blocker shortcuts are not covered by its current cases. Ran focused policy tests, CLI publication race coverage, go vet, both strict validation commands, artifact-check, surface-check, context resolution, suggest-review, diff whitespace checks, and final Git status. New counterexamples are established by source inspection, not claimed as newly executed regression tests. Both full validation runs failed; their failures are not attributed to these source findings without further evidence. No repository changes or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared implementation claims with the spec, ADR, code, and executed checks. Distinguished passing focused tests and sealed evidence from source-derived counterexamples and current failed gates. The cause of the full-validation failures remains unresolved. Writers respecting engine locks are an explicit operating assumption; no finding is accepted as a risk.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected guarded close publication, ExpectAbsent receipt publication, intent ordering, and conflict handling. The targeted CLI publication test also passed under the race detector; no separate concurrency defect was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N11\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The public closeout/MCP terminal projection can discard a genuine child blocker.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N12\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Unresolved explicit Markdown association targets can silently become absence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N14\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Federated source proof can accept a receipt-backed terminal result that repeated CLI close rejects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N12\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Missing association knowledge is not surfaced through the evaluator's diagnostics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N16\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Adoption changes the terminal state of an independently approved historical milestone under an active roadmap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N10\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exempt aggregate review currently permits an unjudged multi-member milestone exit gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-89a10c4a9871f35f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The accepted design separates mandatory explicit close from aggregate review cost through deterministic thresholds and an immutable receipt. A shared evaluator, schema-versioned adoption, and local explicit ADR associations address that cause. The findings concern incomplete enforcement of this selected design.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-607ff681\",\n          \"basis\": \"R3\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template adds adrs: so an explicit ADR association can participate in the deterministic when-justified predicate.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The accepted ADR records policy location, modes, defaults, deterministic thresholds, and historical compatibility before implementation.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English and pt-BR manuals, embedded mirrors, roadmap templates, adoption flags, and receipt descriptions. Thresholds, policy syntax, explicit close, defaults, and prospective adoption are consistently documented. Runtime enforcement defects are reported separately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N13\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reached and attention projections can suppress a scope whose child-terminal verifier is nonterminal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N10\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required preservation of exit gates under aggregate-review exemption is not fulfilled.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N15\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A governed implementation modification is absent from the approved artifact declaration and fails both strict delivery gates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N9\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A contract-changing scope can bypass the protected baseline's mandatory-human overlay.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-89a10c4a9871f35f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing capability adoption and one evaluator is smaller than introducing a settings subsystem or agent judgment. Receipts are justified by the required explicit milestone transition. Local association inventory avoids speculative global discovery and adds no external dependency. A future requirement for remote backlink discovery would invalidate this bounded association design and require another decision.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed, exit 1: artifact.claims=39, artifact.observed=73, artifact.findings=927. The JSON rerun confirms one error: undeclared pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go; the other findings are warnings. This command loads a recorded change set ending at fe2013c7; direct inspection of the requested sealed range independently confirms the same undeclared modification. See N15.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-89a10c4a9871f35f\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not execute assessment producers under the no-write boundary. Reviewed the sealed structural evidence, current diff, spec, ADR, and both material structural mappings directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not 